{
  "_about": [
    "Golden cases for the self-note bodies and the history hand-off document a device sends its account's own new device.",
    "Self-notes: docs/sealed-messages.md §Self-notes.",
    "The hand-off: docs/sealed-messages.md §Handing history to your own new device.",
    "The sealing of a self-note is pinned in mls/fixtures/account-store.json; this table pins what is inside.",
    "Parsing is all this table pins. A pointer whose key is not sealed to the device (`k` or `key` with no `kb`) parses as below and imports nothing: the reader opens only `kb` (docs/sealed-messages.md §Handing history to your own new device).",
    "`note`: `wire` is a self-note's plaintext. `expect` is null when the reader must ignore it (never an error), else one of {kind: read, g, m, at}, {kind: transfer, ptr, f}, {kind: none, f}, {kind: receipts, g, rc} or {kind: history, d, f}. `ptr` is passed through untouched, a `kb` in it included: the hand-off's key sealed to the device it went to, which that device opens in place of `k` (the box is pinned in mls/fixtures/account-store.json).",
    "`parse`: `wire` is the decrypted hand-off document. `expect` is null when it is not a document the reader may read, else the conversations to import. A conversation with no `g`, and a message missing `id`, `by` or `at`, or with neither `text` nor attachments, is dropped and the rest survive. `i`, `r` and `read` default to \"\", `b` to false; unknown keys are ignored.",
    "In a message, `id` is the envelope id, `i`, `r` and `b` the frame's id, reply parent and broadcast flag, `at` epoch milliseconds, and `a` the frame's attachment pointers, passed through. An entry of `a` that is not an object is dropped; an `a` that is not an array is none. A pointer with no `o` or no `k` is an attachment the approver could not hand over.",
    "`rc` maps a reader's actor id to {r, d}, the read and delivered marks that reader sent, oldest first. Each list keeps its non-empty strings once each, in order, then its newest 16. Present (even {}) means the approver knew; absent means it did not.",
    "`p` lists the conversation's members as the approver holds them (non-strings and empties dropped, a repeat kept once). `q` is true only for an unanswered message request.",
    "`f` is the hand-off's format: 1 for words only, 2 with attachments and receipts, 3 with reactions (`re`). A value that is not a positive integer, or none, reads as 1. In the `history` note, `f` is the format the asking device holds, a whole number or else 0.",
    "In `expect`, an absent `a` means [], `p` means [], `q` means false, and `rc` means absent.",
    "To replay: run each case through your own implementation of the format and compare the result with the case's expectation, field by field."
  ],
  "version": 1,
  "cases": [
    {
      "name": "an ordinary sentence is not a transfer",
      "call": "parse",
      "wire": "see you at nine",
      "expect": null
    },
    {
      "name": "another peachy kind is not a transfer",
      "call": "parse",
      "wire": "{\"peachy\":\"history\",\"v\":2}",
      "expect": null
    },
    {
      "name": "an unknown version is not a transfer this build may read",
      "call": "parse",
      "wire": "{\"peachy\":\"transfer\",\"v\":2,\"conversations\":[]}",
      "expect": null
    },
    {
      "name": "conversations must be an array",
      "call": "parse",
      "wire": "{\"peachy\":\"transfer\",\"v\":1,\"conversations\":{}}",
      "expect": null
    },
    {
      "name": "an empty transfer is a transfer",
      "call": "parse",
      "wire": "{\"peachy\":\"transfer\",\"v\":1,\"conversations\":[]}",
      "expect": {
